s.e:
No; thou’rt a fool, I'll swear, if e’re thou grant;
Much of my veneration thou must want,
When once thy kindness puts my ignorance out;
For a learn’d Age is…

What time the mighty moon was gathering light
Love paced the thymy plots of Paradise,
And all about him roll'd his lustrous eyes;

Spring, tire, axle, and linchpin too,
Steel of the finest, bright and blue;
Thoroughbrace bison-skin, thick and wide;
Boot, top, dasher, from tough old…

shall then that thing that honours thee―
how miserable a Thing soever, yet a Thing still ;
and though a Thing of nothing, thy Thing ever
